achilles:
The length'ning line moves languishing along.
When great Patroclus courts Achilles' aid,
The grateful tribute of my tears is paid;

aches:
To buy your life is nearly impossible,
Being sold away to Lamia. My head aches;
I cannot see my road along this dark;

achin:
Dese eyes o' mine is wringin' wet;
My haht's a-achin' ha'd an' so',
De way hit nevah ached befo';

achime:
With some new spirit seems to thrill;
And all the temple bells achime.
Ring out the glee of Christmas time.
